        "id": 7617,
        "name": "Zalrus9",
        "username": "Zalrus9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/zalrus9/{size}/2124_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-07T22:26:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey all! So I usually play Sentinels solo, and because I like listening to something, I've been want to listen to pandora when I do so. &nbsp;I said this in another post, but I found myself listening to \"Over the rainbow/ What a wonderful world\" when I was fighing Iron Legacy, and I found the juxtapositon to be rather dissonant, and slightly beautiful at the same time, especially with the card \"former allies.\" I thought if anybody else has any sort of playlist to a particular villan. I've thought up a bit of a list for me:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Iron Legacy - Israel \"What a wonderful world/ Over the Rainbow,\" also probably \"Requiem for a dream?\"</p>\n<p>The Dreamer - \"Paradise\" by Coldplay. Again, that's another rather dissonant one, but I think the ethereal quality of the vocals matches the otherworldly quality of the people the heroes fight.</p>\n<p>La Capitan - May be a bit cliche, but the Pirates of the Caribean is quite good, I hear... Although if you're old school, Pirates of Penzance is rather campy enough to fit the theme of a time travelling pirate</p>\n<p>Spite - I find the \"Hotline Miami\" soundtrack to be rather good fit, because the main character of that video game, much like spite, is on a drug-fueled killing spree, and the 80s Techno-Synth vibes portray that beautifully.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>That's all I've got now. Do you listen to anything special when you get your game on?&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:56.876Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
